---
/*
  ═══ Philosophy — six convictions (BRIEF §7) ═══

  CE N'EST PAS UNE ETUDE DE CAS, et le gabarit ne s'y applique donc pas tel
  quel. Pas de chiffres cles - cette page n'en a aucun a donner -, pas de trois
  temps : six convictions, qui ne se racontent pas l'une apres l'autre mais se
  tiennent ensemble.

  LA COMPOSITION PORTE LES SIX, et c'est la generalisation naturelle du
  dispositif de Language : six cases Mondrian de tailles differentes, chacune
  une conviction, chacune qui s'ouvre sous la grille. Le lecteur voit les six
  d'un coup d'oeil et ouvre celle qui l'interesse - au lieu de derouler six
  blocs qu'on lit dans l'ordre ou qu'on saute.

  LES CARTES N'ONT PAS DE SYNTHESE, et c'est propre a cette page : le titre EST
  la conviction, complete en elle-meme. Lui ajouter un resume la redirait en
  moins bien. Voir la prop `synthese` de CarteDossier.

  TOUT LE TEXTE EST CONSERVE : les six intitules, les six titres et les neuf
  paragraphes de l'ancienne page sont la, mot pour mot.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/etude.css';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import CarteDossier from '../components/CarteDossier.astro';
import Bouton from '../components/Bouton.astro';

/*
  Les six convictions. L'ordre n'est pas indifferent : il va de ce qui precede
  le systeme (comprendre) a ce qui lui survit (la relation au courant), en
  passant par la methode, le cadre, le point et la fondation. Le rang vient du
  tableau, donc reordonner renumerote.

  `aire` est le grid-area de la case ; les couleurs suivent le rythme Mondrian
  et non le rang - deux rouges voisins seraient une rangee, pas une
  composition.
*/
const convictions = [
  { cle: 'premise', intitule: 'The premise', couleur: 'rouge' as const,
    titre: 'Understanding comes before the system.',
    aire: '1 / 1 / 3 / 3', large: true },
  { cle: 'method', intitule: 'The method', couleur: 'bleu' as const,
    titre: 'Communication at the core, from brief to ship.',
    aire: '1 / 4 / 2 / 6' },
  { cle: 'frame', intitule: 'The frame', couleur: 'jaune' as const,
    titre: "A system doesn't standardize people. It frees them.",
    aire: '2 / 4 / 4 / 6' },
  { cle: 'point', intitule: 'The point', couleur: 'bleu' as const,
    titre: "What's left is what matters.",
    aire: '3 / 1 / 4 / 3' },
  { cle: 'foundation', intitule: 'The foundation', couleur: 'rouge' as const,
    titre: "Care isn't the soft part. It's the foundation.",
    aire: '4 / 1 / 5 / 4' },
  { cle: 'current', intitule: 'The current', couleur: 'jaune' as const,
    titre: "I don't work against the current. I learn to ride it.",
    aire: '4 / 4 / 5 / 7' },
].map((c, i) => ({ ...c, rang: String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0') }));
---
<Base
  title="Philosophy - Léa Giezek"
  description="Six convictions behind the systems I build, and the care that keeps them alive - on conviction, delivery, and the teams that carry both."
>

  <Hero
    courant="philosophy"
    eyebrow="Philosophy · What I hold"
    filigrane="Philosophy"
  >
    Six convictions behind the systems, and the care that keeps them alive.
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Anything can be systematized, once you truly understand each craft. I
      believe people move systems forward - not the other way around. Built on
      trust over control, and humility. Not a system someone maintains, but one
      a whole community owns, defends, and grows.
      <b>Never alone. Conviction over caution, always.</b>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <div class="etude">

    {/*
      ─── La composition des six convictions ───
      Six colonnes, quatre rangees, deux colonnes fines (la 3 et la 6) qui ne
      portent que du decor : ce sont elles qui empechent les six cases de se
      lire comme un tableau. Les rangees sont des planchers et non des
      hauteurs, pour la meme raison que sur les trois etudes - une conviction
      qui gagne une ligne fait grandir sa rangee au lieu d'etre rognee.
    */}
    <div class="compo" id="composition" data-grille>
      {convictions.map((c, i) => (
        <>
          <CarteDossier
            id={`carte-${c.cle}`}
            rang={c.rang}
            intitule={c.intitule}
            titre={c.titre}
            couleur={c.couleur}
            commande={`pan-${c.cle}`}
            large={c.large}
            aire={c.aire}
          />
          {/* les deux colonnes fines, posees apres la premiere et la deuxieme
              carte pour que l'ordre du DOM reste celui de la lecture */}
          {i === 0 && (
            <>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:1 / 3 / 2 / 4"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--gris"></span></div>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:2 / 3 / 3 / 4"></div>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:3 / 3 / 4 / 4"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--noir"></span></div>
            </>
          )}
          {i === 1 && (
            <>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:1 / 6 / 2 / 7"></div>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:2 / 6 / 3 / 7"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--rouge"></span></div>
              <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:3 / 6 / 4 / 7"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--gris"></span></div>
            </>
          )}
        </>
      ))}
    </div>

    {/* ═══════════ 01 · The premise ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-premise" aria-labelledby="titre-premise">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-premise">01 &middot; The premise</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">Understanding comes <em class="em-rouge">before the system.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>Not by putting experts in a room together. By understanding each craft deeply enough to translate it to the others. Systematization isn't the cause - it's what becomes possible once the understanding is there.</p>
            <p>That's why my path runs through <strong>brand, retail, agency and product</strong>: I don't systematize what I haven't understood, and you don't understand a craft you haven't practiced - or at least dived deep enough into it to get along and speak the same language.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Bouton variante="bleu" class="suite" commande="carte-method">Next: the method →</Bouton>
    </section>

    {/* ═══════════ 02 · The method ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-method" aria-labelledby="titre-method">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-method">02 &middot; The method</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">Communication at the core, <em class="em-bleu">from brief to ship.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>In 2018, communication was my <em>subject</em> - I systematized how 2,500 people talked about IT. With Elements, communication became my <em>method</em> - I systematized digital products by making brand, design and engineering finally understand each other. <strong>The subject moved from communication to product. The method never did.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Bouton variante="bleu" class="suite" commande="carte-frame">Next: the frame →</Bouton>
    </section>

    {/* ═══════════ 03 · The frame ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-frame" aria-labelledby="titre-frame">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-frame">03 &middot; The frame</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">A system doesn't standardize people. <em class="em-rouge">It frees them.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>The fear every craftsperson has of a system is that it will flatten them - make them interchangeable. The opposite is true. A good system carries the repeatable, so real expertise has room to breathe. The pivot was never rigidity; it was flexibility, and the collaboration with every stakeholder that made the whole thing rich. <strong>You systematize the frame that frees the craft. You don't replace the craft.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Bouton variante="bleu" class="suite" commande="carte-point">Next: the point →</Bouton>
    </section>

    {/* ═══════════ 04 · The point ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-point" aria-labelledby="titre-point">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-point">04 &middot; The point</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">What's left <em class="em-bleu">is what matters.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>People doing the work that actually creates value - faster, yes, but mostly more <em>confident</em> in what they make, their core expertise valued instead of spent on what a system should have carried. Trusted to own their craft, and accountable for it. That's the point. Not adoption metrics. <strong>People who trust what they ship.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Bouton variante="bleu" class="suite" commande="carte-foundation">Next: the foundation →</Bouton>
    </section>

    {/* ═══════════ 05 · The foundation ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-foundation" aria-labelledby="titre-foundation">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-foundation">05 &middot; The foundation</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">Care isn't the soft part. <em class="em-rouge">It's the foundation.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>A team that isn't well can't shine, and can't ship. So I hold the health of a team - its wellbeing, its inclusion, its safety to speak - with the <strong>same force</strong> I hold conviction and delivery.</p>
            <p>But care doesn't stop at the team. It runs the whole length of a system's life: <strong>care for the people who build it, care for the people who use it, care for the people it ultimately reaches</strong> - the practitioner leaning on the library, and the patient on the other side of the screen.</p>
            <p>A system is only as strong as the people who own it, and it only stays alive because it passes, with care, from one set of hands to the next. <strong>Inclusion isn't a value I add on top. It's infrastructure.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Bouton variante="bleu" class="suite" commande="carte-current">Next: the current →</Bouton>
    </section>

    {/* ═══════════ 06 · The current ═══════════ */}
    <section class="pan" id="pan-current" aria-labelledby="titre-current">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="titre-current">06 &middot; The current</h2>
      <div class="subsec">
        <div class="split">
          <p class="lead">I don't work against the current. <em class="em-bleu">I learn to ride it.</em></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p>When AI arrived, I didn't brace against it - I learned its temper first: explore, listen, build the trust, then move. You don't tame a force you don't understand. <strong>You earn the right to ride it - guardrails first, then the speed.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="closing">
        <h2>Never alone. <em class="em-bleu">Conviction over caution, always.</em></h2>
        <p class="cbody">These six aren't a manifesto I wrote after the fact - they're what the work keeps proving. If you want to see them running at scale, the three studies are where they show.</p>
        <Bouton variante="bleu" href="/system-practice-elements">See them at work →</Bouton>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* ═══ Ce qui est propre a Philosophy ═══ */

  /*
    LA COMPOSITION DES SIX CONVICTIONS. Six colonnes, quatre rangees. Les
    colonnes 3 et 6 sont fines et ne portent que du decor : ce sont elles qui
    empechent les six cases de se lire comme un tableau a deux colonnes.

    Rangees en minmax, pour la raison mesuree a l'etape 4 : en pixels fixes,
    une conviction qui gagne une ligne entre 861 et 1120 est AVALEE par la
    carte, qui est en overflow:hidden.

    Au-dessus du point de rupture seulement : etude.css remet la composition
    sur une colonne sous 860px, et cette declaration vit plus loin dans le
    bundle - a specificite egale elle gagnerait, media query comprise.
  */
  @media(min-width:861px){
    .compo{grid-template-columns:26fr 20fr 6fr 24fr 18fr 6fr;
      grid-template-rows:minmax(180px,auto) minmax(130px,auto)
        minmax(150px,auto) minmax(160px,auto)}
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initDossier } from '../scripts/dossier';
  initDossier();
</script>
